i le 0.9 per cent \nvincristine  sulphate RS in water \t\n• w/v(-s-olution of Sodium Chloride, immediately before use\nRejerOce solution  (d). Dilute 1.0 ml of reference solution0\n4)26.0 ml with  water.\n3492\nThe constituted solution complies with the requirements for \nClarity of solution and Particulate matter stated under \nParenteral Preparations (Injections).\nStorage. The constituted solution should be used immediately \nafter preparation but, in any case, within the period recom-\nmended by the manufacturer.\nVincristine Injection contains not less than 90.0 per cent and \nnot more than 110.0 per cent of the stated amount of vincristine \nsulphate, C46H561\\14010,H2SO4•\nUsual strengths. The equivalent of 1 mg, 2 nig and 5 mg of \ndried vincristine sulphate.\nThe contents of the sealed container  comply  with the \nrequirements stated under Parenteral  Preparations \n(Powders for Injection) and with the  following requirements."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/vincristine-sulphate","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Vincristine Sulphate"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Vincristine Sulphate\n, ... . \n■■ \n: ... Mol. Wt. 923.1\nVincristine Sulphate is methyl (3aÆ,47?,51S',5a7?,l 0b7?;l 3a7?) 4- \nacetoxy-3 a-ethy l-9-[(5S,77?,95)- 5 -ethy 1-5-hydroxy-\nVINCRISTINE SULPHATE\n9- methoxycarbonyl-1,4,5,6,7,8,9,10-octahydro-27/-3 4 7- \nmethanoazacycloundecino[(5,4-b)indbl-9-yl]r6-formyl-5- \nhydroxy- 8-methdxy-3a¿4,5,5a,6,11,12,13a-octahydro- ///- \nindolizino[8,l -¿’¿/jcarbazole-S-carboxylate sulphate.\nVincristine Sulphate contains not less than 95.0 per cent and \nnot more than 104.0 per cent of C^H^h^OithLhSCb, calculated \non the dried basis.\nCategory. Anticancer. • •:: ■ ,w.' w = U r - i. • •; -.: \n.\nDescription. A white to slightly yellowish, amorphous or \ncrystalline powder; very hygroscopic.\nCAUTION— Handle Vincristine Sulphate with; great care \nsince it is a potent cytotoxic agent. Avoid contact with eyes;\nirritant to tissues."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/vinorelbine-injection","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Vinorelbine Injection"},"edition":"ip-2018","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Vinorelbine Injection\nVinorelbine Tartrate Injection\nVinorelbine Injection is a sterile solution of vinorelbine tartrate \nin Water for Injection.\nVinorelbine Injection contains not less than 90.0 per cent and \nnot more than 110.0 per cent of the stated amount of \nvinorelbine, C45H54N408.\nUsual strength. 10 mg per ml.\nDescription. A clear, colourless to pale yellow solution."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/vinorelbine-tartrate","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Vinorelbine Tartrate"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Vinorelbine Tartrate\nC^H^NA, (CAGA \n. . ; Mol Wt. 10.79,1\nVinorelbine.Tartrate is 3 ’,4'-diclehydro-4'-dcoxy- ; . . ; \nC-norvincaleukoblastine ditartrate.. i -, ; - \n<’.\nVinorelbine Tartrate is the ditartrate salt of vinorelbine, a \nsemisynthetic Vinca alkaloid; structurally relate to vinblastine.\nVinorelbine Tanrate contains no t less than 98.0 per cent and \nnot more than 4 02.0 per cent of C45H54NA \ncalculated\non the anhydrous basis. . \ny-,\nCategory.Anticancer. A\"11'’? ' 'A' .\nDescription. A white toy el low orlightbrownamorphous \npowder... ....... ?...................... . \n..... i;. ..\nCAUTION - VinorelbineTarirate is- cytotoxic; extra care \nrequired, to prevent inhaling particles and exposing .the skin- \ntoit. \n. WW ni ■ VÛ y w \nVìi;:-; ?.■:..</ ' ,y GJ;? Î"}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/viper-venom","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Viper Venom"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Viper Venom \n<\nDaboia Venom \n->• ¿/.¿-SS''\nViper Venom is the dried secretion obtained from the poison \nglands of Viperae russelli and other species of Viperae (Fam. \nViperidae). \n... \n;i;,’\nViper Venom contains not less than 50 Mouse Units pet mg."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/volume-of","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Volume of"},"edition":"ip-2018","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Volume of\nAnhydrous\nCategory. Dopamine receptor antagonist; neuroleptic. \nDose. 4 mg to 16 mg.\n, \nM soaium thiosulphate\ndextrose\nconsumed (ml)\n(mg)\nc:\nInject separately the test solution and reference solution (a), \nand record the chromatograms. Measure the responses for \nthe major peak and calculate the content of lactate in the \npreparation under examination.\nj \tr \n8 \n19.8 \n9 \n22.4 \nas \n25.0 \nlib \n11 \n27.6 \nlot \n12 \n30.3 \n\"to- \n13 \n33.0 \n'of \n14 \n35.7\nDescription. A white or yellowish-white, crystalline powder."}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/voriconazole-injection","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Voriconazole Injection"},"edition":"ip-2018","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Voriconazole Injection\nChromatographic system\nVoriconazole Injection is a sterile material consisting of \nVoriconazole with or without buffering agents and other \nexcipients. It is filled in a sealed container.\n-\na stainless steel column 15cm x 4.6 mm, packed with \noctadecysilane bonded to porous silica (3.0 gm). \n-\ncolumn temperature: 35°. \n-\nmobile phase: a mixture of 530 volumes of a buffer \nsolution prepared by dissolving 1.9 g of ammonium \n_formate in 1000 ml of water, adjusted to pH 4.0 with \nformic acid, 157 volumes of acetonitrile and 313\nflow rate: 1 ml per minute, \nconductivity detector, use a self-regenerating anion \nsuppressor, \n-\ninjection volume: 20 gl.\nThe injection is constituted by dissolving the contents of the \nsealed container in the requisite amount of the liquid stated \non the label, immediately before use.\nThe relative retention time with reference to voriconazole\nThe constituted solution complies with the requirements for \nClarity of solution and Particulate matter stated under \nParenteral Preparations (Injections).\nimpurity E (retention time: about 4 minutes) for chloride is \nabout 1.5. \nInject reference solutions (b) and (c). The test is not valid \nunless in the chromatogram obtained with reference solution \n(b) the resolution between the peaks due to voriconazole \nimpurity E and chloride is not less than 3.5 and in the \nchromatogram obtained with reference solution (c) the tailing \nfactor for the peak due to voriconazole impurity E is not more \nthan 1.7. \nInject reference solution (c) and the test solution. Run the \nchromatogram twice the retention time of the peak due to \nvoriconazole impurity E. The area of any peak due to \nvoriconazole impurity E is not more than the area of the \nprincipal peak in the chromatogram obtained with reference \nsolution (c) (0.1 per cent).\nvolumes of methanol, \nflow rate: 1.4 ml per minute, \n-\nspectrophotometer set at 256 nm, \n-\ninjection volume: 20g1. \nName \nRelative \nretention time\nStorage. The constituted solution should be used immediately \nafter preparation but, in any case, within the period \nrecommended by the manufacturer.\nCorrection\nfactor\nVoriconazole Injection contains not less than 90.0 per cent \nand not more than 110.0 per cent of the stated amount of \nvoriconazole, C I6H 14F3N50.\nImpurity A' \n0.25 \n0.7 \nImpurity B2 \n0.6 \n2.1 \nImpurity C3 \n0.3 \n0.7"}},{"@id":"https://www.openphar.org/data/ip/monographs/voriconazole","@type":"IndexedMonograph","prefLabel":{"en":"Voriconazole"},"edition":"ip-2022","category":"monographs","definition":{"en":"Voriconazole\nCi6H14F3N5O ,.:.v \n...A \n..Z . Mol.wt.3493\nVoriconazole is (27?,35')-2-(2,4-difiuofbptieriyI)-;3'(5'\nfluoropyimridin^-yOH^lHhl^A-triazdl-T^y^butari-ZAjIkf^c\nVoriconazole contains hot less than 97.5 per; cent and not \nmore' than 102.0 per cent of CieHulSNsO, calculated bn the \nanhydrous basis/ ; \ny '■